{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/931396-sidereals-wfhl-enemies-of-heaven-aberration-of-fate-the-traveller-in-black","id":931396,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Enemies of Heaven - Aberration of Fate, the Traveller in Black","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-14T09:06:53-07:00","id":931396,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Enemies of Heaven - Aberration of Fate, the Traveller in Black","content":"<b>The Traveller in Black</b><br /> <br /> He bears a staff of yellow-white wood, and all the subtle whorls look like the skin of unfresh cream; it shifts as he walks, like fog and dust trapped in a beam of moonlight. From crown to toe he is robed in fuligin, save a mask of white jade and gloves of supple white leather. He has many names and one, one nature but many. He is the bane of chaos and the ruin of gods, serving his particular order. He is bound by inscrutable laws, and free of common constraint. He grants what you wish, but rarely what you want and never what you need.<br /> <br /> The first reported sighting of the Traveller in Black date to the Contagion, when the tide of chaos swept across the face of Creation and the Fair Folk's crusade against shape seemed most likely to come to fruition. Since that time, appearances have been scattered and unusual, generally accompanying a significant derailment of fate due to the actions of beings from beyond Heaven's ken or in flagrant violation of the plans of Destiny. When confronted, the Traveller asserts that he is a servant of All, come to bring order from disorder. Whatever the truth of his intentions, his actions give the lie; things may be ordered in his wake, but they are ordered to an alien sensibility with no relation to the nature of Creation.<br /> <br /> Unlike some aberrations, the Traveller in Black is almost always a bane to the Sidereals. Although he often remedies the immediate cause of some cause of a failure of fate, the cure is often worse than the disease. In the wake of the Traveller, fire burns cold, rooms reorder themselves via higher dimensional math, and the senses are intermixed, giving rise to loud colors, red sounds and numeric smells. Sometimes, the Traveller can be pointed at some more pressing problem where his presence can be turned to good- but convincing the alien aberration to change course is never an easy task.<br /> <br /> <b>Essence:</b> 5, <b>Willpower:</b> 10, <b>Join Battle:</b> 8 dice<br /> <b>Personal Motes:</b> 100<br /> <b>Health Levels:</b> -0x2/-1x4/-2x4/-4x2/Incap.<br /> <b>Actions:</b> Feats of Strength: 7 dice (can attempt Strength 5 feats), Recognize Wishes: 10 dice, Senses: 8 dice, Social Influence: 8 dice<br /> Appearance: 2, Resolve: 6, Guile: 7<br /> <br /> <b>Combat</b><br /> Attack (Staff Strike): 15 dice (Damage: 12)<br /> Attack (Unarmed): 8 dice (Damage: 8)<br /> Combat Movement: 10 dice<br /> Evasion: 5, Parry: 5<br /> Soak/Hardness: 8 / 0<br /> <br /> <i>Merits</i><br /> <br /> <b>One Name and Many:</b> The Traveller in Black arrives with a single Defining Principle. This intimacy cannot be changed or eliminated by non-magical means.<br /> <br /> <b>Many Natures And One:</b> The Traveller in Black has two distinct initiative tracks. He acts on both sets of initiative. When he takes initiative damage, damage is taken from the track with the highest value. The Traveller in Black is only treated as being in Crash if both initiative tracks are crashed. Crashing one of these tracks while the other still has initiative does not grant a break bonus.<br /> <br /> <b>Chill of Cold Iron:</b> The Traveller in Black's person and equipment is treated as cold iron for the purposes of harming and breaking creatures of the Wyld.<br /> <br /> <i>Offensive Charms</i><br /> <br /> <b>Twist of Fate (1m / TN; Reflexive; Instant; Essence 1):</b> The Traveller in Black can reduce the target number of actions he takes by 1 per 1m spent, to a minimum of 5.<br /> <br /> <b>Doubt Denied (8m; Reflexive; Instant; Perilous; Essence 2):</b> The Traveller in Black treats it's Soak as Hardness against an incoming decisive attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Reality Spin (5m; Simple; Instant; Dual; Essence 3):</b> The Traveller in Black attempts to rewrite the reality of someone's existence. If used to make a withering attack- Short range, 12 dice, damage 8 which ignores soak from non-magical sources. If Reality Spin is used to make a decisive attack, 10 dice, and the Traveller does not lose initiative from failed attacks made with Reality Spin. Victims killed by Reality Spin may be transformed in unpredictable and often unsettling ways.<br /> <br /> <i>Miscellaneous Charms</i><br /> <br /> <b>As You Wish (Special):</b> The Traveller in Black may rearrange reality to an almost limitless degree, but only in response to a wish made which aligns with his core Principle. Wishes are rarely granted in a fashion satisfactory to the wisher. Treat this Charm as being the equivalent to Wyld-Shaping Technique (Exalted p. 335), save that the Traveller may use it within Creation. Encounters drawn by use of As You Wish within Creation will tend to consist of elementals and gods investigating the disturbance; Sidereals being dispatched to deal with the Traveller are often stand in for powerful creatures of the Wyld or behemoths. The Traveller in Black rolls 12 dice when using As You Wish.<br /> <br /> <b>So Be It (10m / interval; Simple; Until complete; Essence 5):</b> If a wish is too complex to be granted by a single application of As You Wish, the Traveller in Black may instead opt for the slower but more potent So Be It. This allows the Traveller to perform the equivalent of sorcerous workings of any Ambition, rolling 12 dice per interval. The Traveller does not have a fixed number of intervals before the working fails, but it must commit an additional ten motes per interval it rolls. Each interval requires at least one week of effort. If the Traveller in Black cannot pay the cost for an interval of So Be It before the working is complete, he is destroyed in a scream of silver flame. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T10:00:18-07:00","id":931430,"title":"","content":"My problem with this is that the Traveler in Black works better as an actual Sidereal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T10:05:35-07:00","id":931434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/931396-sidereals-wfhl-enemies-of-heaven-aberration-of-fate-the-traveller-in-black?p=931430#post931430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with this is that the Traveler in Black works better as an actual Sidereal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is part of the reason I like having him as a Sidereal antagonist. He's a figure that walks in from some other story, and starts doing the Sidereal thing sideways.<br /> <br /> The Traveller should make Sidereals feel the same ways Sidereals make everyone else feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T10:31:25-07:00","id":931446,"title":"","content":"I like it! Very frightening, but simple.<br /> <br /> Question: The Essence ratings for some of his powers are a little odd. Usually this doesn't matter, but in a world with powers that let people take spirit charms they meet the prerequisites for when they consume the being, it might be a problem. (Or maybe he doesn't count as a spirit?)<br /> <br /> I'm looking mostly at Reality Spin and Twist of Fate. They both strike me as Essence 4-5 at a minimum.<br /> <br /> I had not considered the two Initiative tracks as a thing to do outside of SPSitV, so that's very clever, and an interesting way to make something like the Traveller in Black more dangerous. What's frightening is that if he just keeps using Reality Spin (which he can given the mote drip) he's like a dynamo that just ramps up and ramps up until his decisive attacks will destroy pretty much anything. I imagine that's intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T10:59:36-07:00","id":931465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/931396-sidereals-wfhl-enemies-of-heaven-aberration-of-fate-the-traveller-in-black?p=931446#post931446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it! Very frightening, but simple.<br /> <br /> Question: The Essence ratings for some of his powers are a little odd. Usually this doesn't matter, but in a world with powers that let people take spirit charms they meet the prerequisites for when they consume the being, it might be a problem. (Or maybe he doesn't count as a spirit?)<br /> <br /> I'm looking mostly at Reality Spin and Twist of Fate. They both strike me as Essence 4-5 at a minimum.<br /> <br /> I had not considered the two Initiative tracks as a thing to do outside of SPSitV, so that's very clever, and an interesting way to make something like the Traveller in Black more dangerous. What's frightening is that if he just keeps using Reality Spin (which he can given the mote drip) he's like a dynamo that just ramps up and ramps up until his decisive attacks will destroy pretty much anything. I imagine that's intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Danke <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I remembered testing a SPSitV and making a mental note of the dual initative track thing as a handy trick for countering the action economy advantage that multiple PCs vs one Big Bad often has to deal with.<br /> <br /> The Traveller is emphatically not a spirit- compare him with Death-in-Life, who is, sort of, a spirit. The Traveller is naturally material and cannot dematerialize. If he's killed, he stays dead (until something else goes seriously fucked up with fate). He's just, ya'know. This guy. (Aberrations are basically their own category of being- the closest thing they compare to is behemoths.)<br /> <br /> (That said, I don't actually think letting a PC get Reality Spin would be that dangerous; the most utilitious ability is to make decisive attacks that don't bleed away your initiative on failures, and I'd say that's a reasonable effect at Essence 3 for 5m a pop).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T11:25:01-07:00","id":931477,"title":"","content":"Though if you wanted, I think the Traveller just doing his thing in the Exalted universe would cause significant problems for the Sidereals. Guy goes around binding irrational, primal, magic forces away from the normal world... cue various gods and elementals &quot;But Traveller in Black (Dynamite), I am an irrational, primal, magical force in the community!&quot;, and fate actually going awry because, yes, (unlike in Travellerverse) the natural order in Exalted does actually need those spirits and that magic to keep running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T11:32:29-07:00","id":931483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/931396-sidereals-wfhl-enemies-of-heaven-aberration-of-fate-the-traveller-in-black?p=931477#post931477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though if you wanted, I think the Traveller just doing his thing in the Exalted universe would cause significant problems for the Sidereals. Guy goes around binding irrational, primal, magic forces away from the normal world... cue various gods and elementals &quot;But Traveller in Black (Dynamite), I am an irrational, primal, magical force in the community!&quot;, and fate actually going awry because, yes, (unlike in Travellerverse) the natural order in Exalted does actually need those spirits and that magic to keep running.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first iteration of him was like this; his staff was basically a limitless Yasal crystal -but I couldn't get it to jibe with the wish-granting element in a fashion I was happy with, and it is a concept that *really* wants to do things that are super no-nos (namely, fucking with the PC's Exaltations).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T11:33:01-07:00","id":931485,"title":"","content":"Theories involving the Traveller in Black:<br /> <br /> 1. The Traveller was once a Sidereal that lost his exaltation somehow. He no longer exists in Fate and his identity has been forgotten, even by himself. <br /> 2. The Traveller is a Third Circle Demon Soul of She Who Lives in Her Name. He travels around bring Order to Chaos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T11:41:04-07:00","id":931490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/931396-sidereals-wfhl-enemies-of-heaven-aberration-of-fate-the-traveller-in-black?p=931465#post931465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(That said, I don't actually think letting a PC get Reality Spin would be that dangerous; the most utilitious ability is to make decisive attacks that don't bleed away your initiative on failures, and I'd say that's a reasonable effect at Essence 3 for 5m a pop).</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely not my hill to die on, but I would imagine it wouldn't be ideal in a situation like this: Use full Awareness Excellency to score a high JB roll, then use Reality Spin at a net mote loss of zero to indefinitely spam all enemies with high initiative decisive attacks. It sounds a bit hinky to me, though I guess it's a good point that it's probably not an issue given that Aberrations are their own kind of being and I don't think PCs can get this power.<br /> <br /> Well. Solars can't, at any rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T11:47:17-07:00","id":931495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/931396-sidereals-wfhl-enemies-of-heaven-aberration-of-fate-the-traveller-in-black?p=931490#post931490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Definitely not my hill to die on, but I would imagine it wouldn't be ideal in a situation like this: Use full Awareness Excellency to score a high JB roll, then use Reality Spin at a net mote loss of zero to indefinitely spam all enemies with high initiative decisive attacks. It sounds a bit hinky to me, though I guess it's a good point that it's probably not an issue given that Aberrations are their own kind of being and I don't think PCs can get this power.<br /> <br /> Well. Solars can't, at any rate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh. He only maintains his initiative on a *failed* decisive attack. A successful decisive attack resets to base as normal.<br /> <br /> I mean- it does mean you can do the 'constantly spam decisive attacks against target Bob' at the opening of the fight, but you were probably going to be doing that anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","user":"wastevens","date":". 07-14-2016, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T12:59:53-07:00","id":931527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/931396-sidereals-wfhl-enemies-of-heaven-aberration-of-fate-the-traveller-in-black?p=931495#post931495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh. He only maintains his initiative on a *failed* decisive attack. A successful decisive attack resets to base as normal.<br /> <br /> I mean- it does mean you can do the 'constantly spam decisive attacks against target Bob' at the opening of the fight, but you were probably going to be doing that anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> OH! Wow, my bad on the reading comprehension botch, I was reading it as not resetting on a successful attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}